# React & Component Patterns

## Component Placement
- **atoms/** — no props drilling beyond 1 level, no hooks, no service calls
- **molecules/** — can accept callback props, use `cn()` for class merging
- **organisms/** — can use `useAuth()` and call services directly if needed
- New UI primitives go in `atoms/` following the existing Radix UI + CVA pattern

## Styling
- Use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils` (clsx + tailwind-merge) for all conditional classes
- Design tokens via CSS variables — never hardcode colors like `text-indigo-600`; use `text-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-card` etc.
- Responsive: always mobile-first. Sidebar hides on mobile (`lg:translate-x-0`).

## Component conventions
```tsx
// ✅ Named exports, forwardRef for atoms
export const Button = React.forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(...)

// ✅ Regular function for pages/organisms
export function BooksPage() { ... }

// ✅ Sub-components at bottom of file, not exported
function BookRow({ record }: { record: BorrowRecord }) { ... }
```

## State & Data Fetching
```tsx
// ✅ Use the hook, not raw supabase in pages
const { books, isLoading, refetch } = useBooks({ search, genreId });

// ❌ Never do this in a page/component
const { data } = await supabase.from("books").select("*");
```

## Auth & Role Gating
```tsx
const { profile, isLibrarian } = useAuth();

// UI gating
{isLibrarian && <Button>Add Book</Button>}

// Route gating — wrap with <LibrarianRoute> in App.tsx
```

## Error Handling
```tsx
// ✅ Services throw, pages/hooks catch and toast
try {
  await bookService.createBook(payload);
  toast.success("Book added");
} catch (err) {
  toast.error(err instanceof Error ? err.message : "Failed to save book");
}
```

## Empty & Loading States
- Loading → `<PageLoader text="..." />` (full page) or `<Skeleton />` (inline)
- Empty → `<EmptyState icon={X} title="..." description="..." action={...} />`
